From fb4010707b40c86c1babc3625e5c5a19ed6f43f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 22:22:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] framerate: live cap from 60, deterministic test runs,
 native-equal loads, VR follows the headset

- The frame rate hooks run in every run that can use them (GA2_FPS is the
  cap the run starts with, 60 = the native cadence; the settings menu
  raises it live up to 240; GA2_FPS_LIVE=0 restores the old behaviour).
  Native with the hooks on matches native without them except a sub-frame
  EE-time difference (one IOP request one iteration earlier in 560 s).
- GA2_FREERUN=1 (test aid): host deadlines count as passed, so guest time
  depends on EE cycles alone; scripted runs (GA2_PAD_SCRIPT) see only the
  script, not the window's input. Two runs of the same script are
  identical however loaded the host is.
- Frame ticks are queued only while the game waits on the frame clock
  (ticks in between are counted from the EE cycle): an idle EE runs the
  IOP up to the next event, and ticks during a load made loads finish
  earlier in EE time than natively (game time drifted 0.69 s ahead of
  voice lines by the battle).
- waitFrameTick(atVBlank): an iteration that overran the game's catch-up
  limit wakes at the next VBLANK, as the native VBLANK wait does, and the
  ticks are realigned to it: the game time lost at loads and scene
  switches is the native amount.
- VR: the cap follows the headset's refresh rate (median of the predicted
  display period; stalls ignored); the window's vsync is off in VR.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
